<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!-- ============================================================================
         HCS VERSION 1 BASELINE, in dcre_hcs, the database this service owns.

         WHAT MOVED AND WHY. public_holiday used to be created in dcre_col, the
         COLLECTIONS family's database, by this service and, racing it, by cde's own
         guard changeset. The owner ruled that out on 2026-08-08: "no, do not write
         public holidays into dcre_col DB. This is a violation of the
         12FactorApp/SOLID". A holiday calendar is not collections data, and a table
         two unrelated contexts can both create is not owned by either.

         hcs is the sole writer (R-04). Readers do not touch this table: they read
         hol_cde_view over their own dedicated read-only datasource, so the physical
         shape below can change without a fleet-wide edit.

         THIS IS A FRESH VERSION 1. Every DCRE database is dropped and recreated, so
         there is deliberately no validCheckSum, no IF NOT EXISTS, and no
         onFail="MARK_RAN" precondition. Those guarded against an already-migrated
         database, and there is none. In particular the cde race that justified the
         old guard cannot recur: cde no longer creates this table anywhere, because
         it no longer shares a database with it.

         The previous form of this changeset was a raw DDL text block, which is the
         vendor-lock the pure-XML rule exists to prevent. It is typed here, with a
         rollback.

         COLUMN NAMING. holiday_date repeats its own host table and by
         rules/be/java/architecture.md should be shortened. It is NOT renamed, and
         this is the one place that decision is actually free to be made, since hcs
         owns the table. The obvious short form is a reserved word in SQL and would
         need quoting at every use site including the published view, so the shortest
         meaningful NON-RESERVED name wins. Recorded rather than silently kept.
         ============================================================================ -->

    <changeSet id="hcs-v1-public-holiday" author="dcre">
        <createTable tableName="public_holiday">
            <column name="id" type="UUID" defaultValueComputed="gen_random_uuid()">
                <constraints primaryKey="true" nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="country" type="VARCHAR(2)">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="holiday_date" type="DATE">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="local_name" type="VARCHAR(128)"/>
            <column name="name" type="VARCHAR(128)"/>
            <column name="is_global" type="BOOLEAN"/>
            <column name="version" type="BIGINT" defaultValueNumeric="0">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="created_at" type="TIMESTAMPTZ" defaultValueComputed="now()">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="updated_at" type="TIMESTAMPTZ" defaultValueComputed="now()">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
        </createTable>
        <addUniqueConstraint tableName="public_holiday" columnNames="country, holiday_date"
                             constraintName="uq_public_holiday_country_date"/>
        <rollback>
            <dropTable tableName="public_holiday"/>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

    <!-- ============================================================================
         THE PUBLISHED CONTRACT. cde reads the calendar through this view and never
         through the table, so hcs keeps the freedom to add columns, backfill, or
         reshape the table without breaking a consumer in another context.

         It is deliberately NARROWER than the table. cde's R-38 process-date roll
         needs a country and a date and nothing else: it asks which dates in a range
         are holidays, and how many are synced for a year. Publishing local_name,
         name, is_global or the audit columns would invite a consumer to depend on
         them, and every such dependency is a future coordinated release.
         ============================================================================ -->

    <changeSet id="hcs-v1-hol-cde-view" author="dcre">
        <createView viewName="hol_cde_view">
            SELECT country, holiday_date FROM public_holiday
        </createView>
        <rollback>
            <dropView viewName="hol_cde_view"/>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
